  planner_response {
    response: "Built **TaskFlow Narrative**, a task and project workflow application aligned with your design system specification (`Plus Jakarta Sans`, cool `#F8FAFC` / `#FFFFFF` surfaces, `#2563EB` primary accents, `#10B981` completion states, and single-level micro-elevation cards).\n\n### Screens & Capabilities Implemented\n- **Today\'s Focus**: Daily summary metrics (`Remaining Today`, `Completed`, `High Priority`, `Planned Focus`), keyboard-first Quick-Add bar with inline due date, priority, and project controls, status/priority filters, and grouped task lists (`Overdue` with one-click reschedule, `Scheduled Today`, and `Completed`).\n- **Upcoming Schedule**: Interactive 7-day workload selector and chronological agenda grouping (`Overdue`, daily sections, and `Unscheduled Backlog`).\n- **Inbox Triage**: Rapid-capture queue for uncategorized items with inline actions to schedule for Today or move directly into a project.\n- **Projects (Portfolio + List & Kanban Board)**: Overview directory with completion progress bars, plus dedicated per-project views supporting both **List** and drag-and-drop **Board** (`To Do`, `In Progress`, `Done`) layouts, project creation, editing, and deletion.\n- **Weekly Review**: Computed completion rate, active queue, completed effort hours, trailing 7-day completion cadence chart, project execution breakdown, and auto-saved weekly narrative reflection notes.\n- **Task Inspector Drawer & Preferences**: Slide-over inspector for editing task titles, workflow status, priority, time estimates, due dates, notes, and nested subtasks; plus a Preferences modal for display name, row density (`Comfortable` / `Compact`), completed-task visibility, JSON backup export, and demo reset.\n- **Persistence & Shortcuts**: All tasks, projects, subtasks, reflection notes, and preferences persist automatically in `localStorage`, with `/` or `Cmd/Ctrl+K` search focus, `Escape` to dismiss overlays, and an undo toast on task deletion.\n\n### Verification\n- `compile_applet` succeeded (`vite` production build passed).\n- `lint_applet` succeeded (`tsc --noEmit` passed with zero errors)."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Successful Compilation**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that both the `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` processes completed successfully on their initial attempts, without any errors. My next step is to rigorously assess the output against the specified requirements, specifically regarding adherence to the **TaskFlow Narrative** design system, including the proper implementation of background surface, card styling and elevations.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "3Tr_arRJlIzbyg-7j8ahAw"
    modified_response: "Built **TaskFlow Narrative**, a task and project workflow application aligned with your design system specification (`Plus Jakarta Sans`, cool `#F8FAFC` / `#FFFFFF` surfaces, `#2563EB` primary accents, `#10B981` completion states, and single-level micro-elevation cards).\n\n### Screens & Capabilities Implemented\n- **Today\'s Focus**: Daily summary metrics (`Remaining Today`, `Completed`, `High Priority`, `Planned Focus`), keyboard-first Quick-Add bar with inline due date, priority, and project controls, status/priority filters, and grouped task lists (`Overdue` with one-click reschedule, `Scheduled Today`, and `Completed`).\n- **Upcoming Schedule**: Interactive 7-day workload selector and chronological agenda grouping (`Overdue`, daily sections, and `Unscheduled Backlog`).\n- **Inbox Triage**: Rapid-capture queue for uncategorized items with inline actions to schedule for Today or move directly into a project.\n- **Projects (Portfolio + List & Kanban Board)**: Overview directory with completion progress bars, plus dedicated per-project views supporting both **List** and drag-and-drop **Board** (`To Do`, `In Progress`, `Done`) layouts, project creation, editing, and deletion.\n- **Weekly Review**: Computed completion rate, active queue, completed effort hours, trailing 7-day completion cadence chart, project execution breakdown, and auto-saved weekly narrative reflection notes.\n- **Task Inspector Drawer & Preferences**: Slide-over inspector for editing task titles, workflow status, priority, time estimates, due dates, notes, and nested subtasks; plus a Preferences modal for display name, row density (`Comfortable` / `Compact`), completed-task visibility, JSON backup export, and demo reset.\n- **Persistence & Shortcuts**: All tasks, projects, subtasks, reflection notes, and preferences persist automatically in `localStorage`, with `/` or `Cmd/Ctrl+K` search focus, `Escape` to dismiss overlays, and an undo toast on task deletion.\n\n### Verification\n- `compile_applet` succeeded (`vite` production build passed).\n- `lint_applet` succeeded (`tsc --noEmit` passed with zero errors)."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 517491168
    }
